meta {
  name: 02 - Get OCR Status & Result
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ocr/status/{{requestId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
}

script:post-response {
  // Keep the document id handy for requests 05, 06, 07 and 11.
  if (res.body && res.body.document && res.body.document.id) {
    bru.setEnvVar("docId", res.body.document.id);
  }
}

docs {
  Polls an asynchronous job. {{requestId}} is set automatically by request 01,
  so run 01 first; otherwise set requestId in the environment by hand.
  
  ## Three possible responses - a polling client must handle all three
  
  PROCESSING - success, request_id, document_id, status, current_page,
  total_pages, percent, message, project_name, user_id, created_at.
  
  WATCH OUT: while processing, `status` is not the bare string "PROCESSING" -
  it carries progress, e.g. "PROCESSING (Page 1 of 1)". Only the submit
  response in request 01 returns a bare "PROCESSING". So poll with a prefix
  test, never equality:
  
      status.startsWith("PROCESSING")
  
  "COMPLETED" and "FAILED" are exact and can be compared directly.
  
  COMPLETED - success, request_id, status, project_name, user_id, and a
  document object holding id, filename, document_type, language,
  processing_time, created_at, completed_at and markdown.
  
  There is no plain_text - it was the same content as markdown with the
  formatting stripped, so it was dropped from the payload. The contract is
  markdown plus structured JSON.
  
  FAILED - success is FALSE, plus request_id, status, error_message,
  project_name, user_id.
  
  ## It DOES return the structured data
  
  `document.structured_data` carries the extracted table (`fields.columns`,
  `fields.rows`, and per document type `fields.items` /
  `fields.summary_totals`). An earlier version of this collection said the
  endpoint returned markdown only; that is no longer true, and no second call
  is needed to get the JSON.
  
  ## ERP shape
  
  Add `?response_format=erp` to get business fields and object-keyed line
  items instead of the `document` block - see request 11. The PROCESSING and
  FAILED responses are unaffected: there is no extracted data to shape yet.
  
  ## Errors
  
  - 400 unrecognised response_format
  - 404 request_id not found
}
